      "name": "vol_return_contrast",
      "expression": "TS_PCTCHANGE($return, 5) - TS_PCTCHANGE($volume, 5)",
      "explanation": "Compares the percentage change in returns and volume over 5 days, exploring timescale contrast."
    },
    {
      "name": "vol_resid",
      "expression": "REGRESI($return, SEQUENCE(60)) - REGRESI($volume, SEQUENCE(60))",
      "explanation": "Subtracts the residual return from the residual volume after removing time trends, exploring residuals."
    },
    {
      "name": "vol_asymmetry",
      "expression": "(TS_PCTCHANGE($return, 10) > 0) ? (TS_ZSCORE($volume, 10)) : (0)",
      "explanation": "Scores volume based on directional return changes, exploring asymmetry."
    },
    {
      "name": "vol_cross_product",
      "expression": "TS_CORR($volume, $return, 20) * TS_MAD($return, 20)",
      "explanation": "Multiplies correlation between volume and return with the MAD of returns, exploring cross-family product."
    },
    {
      "name": "vol_shape_ratio",
      "expression": "TS_SKEW($return, 20) / TS_KURT($return, 20)",
      "explanation": "Ratios skew and kurtosis of returns, exploring shape rather than level."
    }
  ]
}

- Small-cap stocks with unusually high volume on a day see stronger positive returns the next 1-5 days, suggesting retail-driven buying momentum.
- The reversal effect in small-cap stocks after high-volume days is stronger during periods of market stress, indicating behavioral shifts under uncertainty.
- High-volume days in small-cap stocks predict higher returns in the following 30 days, implying that initial overreaction leads to sustained outperformance.

RECIPES
- AXIS: ORDER STATISTICS — the position of the highest return in the top 10% of volume-weighted stocks, relative to the median return of the same group. Uses $return, $volume, window 20.
- AXIS: TIMESCALE CONTRAST — difference between TS_MOMENTUM($close, 5) and TS_MOMENTUM($close, 60), scaled by TS_VOLATILITY($return, 20). Uses $close, $return, windows 5, 60, 20.
- AXIS: NEGLECTED OPERATOR — DECAYLINEAR of $volume over 10 days, divided by the sum of $open prices over 10 days. Uses $volume, $open, window 10.
- AXIS: UNUSUAL PAIRING — TS_CORR($high, $volume, 20) multiplied by the rank of $return within the top 30% of volume. Uses $high, $volume, $return, window 20.
- AXIS: DEPTH — RANK(TS_ZSCORE(TS_PCTCHANGE($close, 5), 20)) nested inside TS_RSI($return, 60). Uses $close, $return, windows 5, 20, 60.
- AXIS: ASYMMETRY — conditional score where $return > 0 and $volume > 1.5 * median($volume), minus the inverse when $return < 0. Uses $return, $volume.
- AXIS: RESIDUAL — REGRESI of $return on $volume over 20 days, then TS_ZSCORE of the residual. Uses $return, $volume, window 20.
- AXIS: CROSS-FAMILY PRODUCT — multiply TS_STD($close, 10) by TS_MAD($return, 20), then divide by the rank of $volume. Uses $close, $return, $volume, windows 10, 20.
- AXIS: SHAPE — the skew of $return distribution over 30 days, normalized by TS_VOLATILITY($close, 60). Uses $return, $close, windows 30, 60.
- AXIS: INVERSION — one minus the ratio of TS_ARGMAX($volume, 20) to TS_ARGMIN($volume, 20), scaled by TS_PCTCHANGE($close, 5). Uses $volume, $close, windows 20, 5.

