RECIPES
- AXIS: ORDER STATISTICS — the position of the maximum daily range within the top 5% of all ranges, calculated as TS_ARGMAX(TS_MAX($high - $low, n), n) divided by TS_COUNT(n)
- AXIS: TIMESCALE CONTRAST — the difference between the 1-day and 30-day standard deviation of the high-low range, using TS_STD($high - $low, 1) minus TS_STD($high - $low, 30)
- AXIS: UNUSUAL PAIRING — the covariance between the high-low range and volume, calculated as TS_COVARIANCE($high - $low, $volume, n)
- AXIS: SHAPE, NOT LEVEL — the skew of the high-low range distribution across 10-day windows, using TS_SKEW($high - $low, 10)
- AXIS: RESIDUAL — the residual from regressing the high-low range against the close price, using REGRESI($high - $low, $close, n)
- AXIS: INVERSION — the negative of the ratio between the high and low prices over 3-day windows, using -($high / $low) where $high and $low are from TS_PCTCHANGE(n=3)
